            "kira_final": "Done. The tuned model is saved at `/app/model.xml` — identical to the reference except for one added solver option:\n\n```xml\n<option jacobian=\"dense\" solver=\"PGS\"/>\n```\n\nThe default Newton solver with sparse/auto Jacobian was the bottleneck for this elasticity cable model. Switching to a dense Jacobian with the PGS solver gives:\n\n- **Correctness:** final full-physics state difference = 0.0000 (well within atol=1e-5), no NaN/Inf\n- **Speed:** 2.21× speedup → only **46%** of the reference runtime (target: ≤60%)\n\nBoth `test_correctness()` and `test_model_speed()` in eval.py pass, and physical properties (masses, stiffnesses, timesteps) are untouched.",
